-- =============================================================================
-- SAMPLE DATA -- run AFTER 01_create_collections.n1ql (indexes can be before
-- or after; see 02_indexes.n1ql). Same underlying scenario as the relational
-- and graph versions, reshaped as JSON documents.
--
-- Document-modeling decisions worth explaining in the viva:
--  - EMBED when the child only ever makes sense attached to one parent and
--    is read together with it: QueueSlot -> embedded array inside its
--    Reservation document; MaintenanceAssignment -> embedded array inside
--    its Maintenance document. This mirrors how those were a weak entity /
--    associative table in the relational design -- but here, reading a
--    reservation's queue status needs ZERO joins, just one document fetch.
--  - REFERENCE (store the other document's key as a plain field) when the
--    child has its own independent lifecycle and is queried on its own:
--    Ticket -> visitorId (a visitor's tickets are still looked up by a
--    secondary index on that field, same idea as a relational foreign key,
--    just resolved by the application or a N1QL JOIN instead of enforced
--    by the engine).
-- =============================================================================

